  "details": "1. Launch VRChat, wearing full-body trackers.\n\n2. Stand in front of a mirror.\n\n3. Enter FBT calibration.\n\n4. Assume a proper calibration pose, but DON'T accept the calibration yet.\n\n5. Look up towards the ceiling, at about a 45-degree angle.\n\n6. Now accept your calibration.\n\n7. Ignoring the mirror, raise your finger to eye level (maybe pointing directly into your eye, maybe parallel with the horizon, something like that).\n\n8. With your hand held like that, notice your reflection in the mirror -- your hand will be BELOW your reflection's eye.\n\n9. To confirm that it isn't just a misconfigured avatar, repeat these steps but look 45 degrees DOWN rather than up in step 5.  The problem should now be very minor.\n\n10. Just to establish that \"just don't look up\" isn't a great solution, repeat again but look straight forward in step 5.  Notice that the problem still exists!  It's subtler than looking up, but still noticeably incorrect.   \"Always look downwards during calibration\" seems to function as a workaround, but most players won't know to do this.",
